    "lawCode": "Amd §§88, 89-a & 89-b, Nav L",
    "lawSection": "Navigation Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5482\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the navigation law, in relation to\nclarifying the continuity of a deck of a vessel for the determination\nof pilotage units used in calculating pilotage fees\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL : To clarify the continuity of deck\nof a vessel for the determination of pilotage units used in\ncalculating pilotage fees.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS : This legislation amends paragraph\n(c) of subdivision 4 of §88 of the navigation law as added by Chapter\n197 of the laws of 1990.\n\n JUSTIFICATION : This bill proposes to amend the navigation law in\nrelation to clarifying the continuity of a deck of a vessel for the\ndetermination of pilotage units used in calculating pilotage fees by\nrecognizing that vessel construction evolves with time, technology and\nneed. Today's innovations in naval architecture were simply not\nenvisioned when the language of the original statute was written, and\nas such needs to be updated.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY : New bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS : None.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE : Immediately.\n",
